Subject: [PATCH] T23: preserve normal ISP links when bypass is disabled

EnableSensor already creates the normal ISP links on T23. Calling
IMP_ISP_Tuning_SetISPBypass(DISABLE) later is not a no-op: libimp stops
streaming, destroys those links and recreates link configuration 1. With
the SC2336P this leaves sizeimage zero and every frame buffer is rejected.

Keep the sensor-enabled pipeline for normal T23 capture. Preserve the
existing explicit bypass request and all other platforms' behavior.

Upstream: Pending

diff --git a/src/IMPSystem.cpp b/src/IMPSystem.cpp
--- a/src/IMPSystem.cpp
+++ b/src/IMPSystem.cpp
@@ -438,6 +438,16 @@ int IMPSystem::init() {
-  ret = hal::isp::set_isp_bypass(cfg->image.isp_bypass);
-  LOG_DEBUG_OR_ERROR(ret, "hal::isp::set_isp_bypass(" << cfg->image.isp_bypass
-                                                      << ")");
+#if defined(PLATFORM_T23)
+  // EnableSensor has already established the normal ISP pipeline.
+  // Even disabling whole-ISP bypass tears down and recreates its links
+  // in the T23 SDK, leaving the frame-source format uninitialized.
+  if (!cfg->image.isp_bypass) {
+    LOG_DEBUG("T23: retaining normal ISP links (bypass disabled)");
+  } else
+#endif
+  {
+    ret = hal::isp::set_isp_bypass(cfg->image.isp_bypass);
+    LOG_DEBUG_OR_ERROR(ret, "hal::isp::set_isp_bypass(" << cfg->image.isp_bypass
+                                                        << ")");
+  }
-
+
   ret = hal::isp::set_anti_flicker(cfg->image.anti_flicker);
   LOG_DEBUG_OR_ERROR(ret, "hal::isp::set_anti_flicker("
